The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second word) instead of `parts[0]` (the first word). This caused it to return 'world' instead of 'hello' for the input 'hello world', and crash with an IndexError for single-word inputs like 'solo'.

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split array.
